Practical philosophy

        (1) by a truth of practical logic, absent knowledge of whether ∃ a ground (stable ground)
          and, if so, what it consists in, that knowledge (ground knowledge) is itself
          a ground (the default ground)
            : re `^*\(\d+\) (.+)`s see `^*argue\+ that, ${same}`p @ default/._/text.notes.brec
        (2) despite long efforts [in the past], ultimately|{in the end} {we have}|{∃ among us}
          (at present) no settled consensus on the ground question or its likes
            : re `the ground question` sc. `whether ∃ a ground.+and.+what it consists in`s
        (3) we know|have (at present) of no way|method to [reliably]
          {gauge|determine|predict an upper limit|bound on}|bound
          {how long}|{the period|{length of time}} it could|might take to acquire ground knowledge
          or deal with any stable ground we thereby apprehend

        : see `^*\(1\)`
        : see `^*\(2\)`
        : see `^*\(3\)` :
       ────────────────
        (4) [practical] reason/logic directs us to carry on for a period [of time] that would
           (in [our] [present] prospect|outlook) be open-ended and likely long

        (5) a safehold highly fit to secure the long-term survival of mind-bearing populations
          extends throughout the cosmos
            : ad `long-term` : over periods on the scale of cosmogonal time,
              as opposed to the (relatively short) scale of geogenic time
                : re `scale of cosmogonal time`
                  see `stability on the longer ${same}` @ ~/work/safehold/40.observation.brec
                : re `\(relatively short\) scale of geogenic time`
                  see `the scope.+not restricted to.+the ${same}`s @ ~/work/safehold/40.observation.brec
            : re `(a safehold.+to secure the.+survival of) (mind)-bearing (populations)`p
              see `${1} ${3} of beings \(like us\) that have ${2}`p @ ~/work/safehold/40.observation.brec

        : see `^*\(4\)`
        : see `^*\(5\)` :
       ────────────────
        (6) the safehold’s fitness as a means coincides with the end to which reason/logic
          (in [our] [present] prospect|outlook) directs us

    - any explanation for the|this coincidence must lie in the aetiology of the safehold [itself]
